{"title":"04 Features: 53 measures from text","description":"extract_linguistic_features turns speech text into numeric measures.","nextTour":"05 Analysis: group differences and MoCA","steps":[{"file":"src/delware_speech/features.py","line":24,"title":"Lazy model globals","description":"`_NLP`, `_STOPWORDS`, `_COMMON_WORDS` start as None/empty and load on first use — importing the package is cheap and each model loads exactly once per process."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/features.py","line":46,"title":"SpaCy with self-heal","description":"`get_nlp()` loads `en_core_web_sm`; if the model is missing it downloads it first (lines 53–55). The OSError you get mid-run without the pre-fetch never happens here — it just costs time on first use."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/features.py","line":91,"title":"Richness: TTR, Brunét, Honoré","description":"`calculate_lexical_richness` works on content tokens (stopwords removed). Brunét's index is line 103 (`V / N^0.165`); Honoré's statistic uses hapax counts (lines 106–113)."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/features.py","line":118,"title":"WordNet depth","description":"`calculate_hypernym_count` = mean minimum hypernym-tree depth over noun/verb synsets — the paper's lexical-sophistication proxy. Wrapped in try/except, returns 0.0 on any failure."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/features.py","line":133,"title":"Cohesion as overlap","description":"`calculate_cohesion_score` = mean Jaccard overlap (line 149) of consecutive sentence token sets — the Halliday & Hasan cohesion operationalization."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/features.py","line":157,"title":"Counting disfluencies","description":"`count_disfluencies` matches the DISFLUENCIES list (line 28) as whole words via `\\b` boundaries — kept possible at all because the CHAT cleaner preserves filled pauses."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/features.py","line":163,"title":"The 53-feature entry point","description":"`extract_linguistic_features(text)` — pure function, no I/O, same 63 output keys for every input. Everything below is its internal order; the returned dict at line 343 is the frame schema."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/features.py","line":168,"title":"Empty text short-circuit","description":"Empty/blank input returns `_empty_feature_dict()` (line 415): a zeroed dict with the full key set, so downstream frames always share columns."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/features.py","line":197,"title":"POS counts from SpaCy","description":"One SpaCy pass feeds everything: coarse POS counts (line 197) and fine tags (line 198) drive the rate features, deixis, and tense rates later."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/features.py","line":219,"title":"Open vs closed class","description":"`ocw` = verbs+nouns+adjectives+adverbs; `ccw` is the complement; `open_class_words_rate` and `content_density` come straight from these."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/features.py","line":260,"title":"The paper's complexity formula","description":"`syntactic_complexity = (2·conjunctions + 2·pronouns + nouns + verbs) / total` — the exact Nyongesa formula; `ref_r_real` (noun/verb ratio) sits next to it."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/features.py","line":264,"title":"Clauses and passive voice","description":"Dependency-label counts: subordinate clauses (`advcl`, `relcl`, `ccomp`, …) at line 264; passive constructions (`nsubjpass`, `auxpass`, VBN tags) at line 267."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/features.py","line":271,"title":"Readability, per-metric guards","description":"Each textstat metric is its own try/except (dale_chall shown; flesch, coleman_liau, ari, gunning_fog, syllables, reading_time follow). A failing metric yields 0.0, never a crash."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/features.py","line":302,"title":"Sentiment via TextBlob","description":"Polarity and subjectivity from TextBlob — the semantic block of the feature set, guarded the same way."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/features.py","line":314,"title":"The three deixis rates","description":"Personal deixis from pronoun tags (line 314); spatial from LOC/GPE/FAC/ORG entities + SPATIAL_WORDS (lines 318–320); temporal from DATE/TIME entities + TEMPORAL_WORDS (lines 323–325)."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/features.py","line":328,"title":"Tense rates","description":"Verb total = verbs + auxiliaries (line 328); past = VBD+VBN, present = VBP/VBZ/VBG/VB, future = will/shall/gonna (and `going to`) markers — lines 329–341."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/features.py","line":415,"title":"The zeroed schema","description":"`_empty_feature_dict` enumerates every key explicitly — this list IS the schema contract; add a feature here and in the main return together."}]}